{"id": "27d0226b-8f3c-49a3-a8a0-dd5339d925a0", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The AWS documentation on MediaConnect monitoring lists flow source monitoring, CloudTrail, EventBridge, and CloudWatch metrics, but doesn't mention native CloudWatch Logs as an official vended log source. A blog post seems to suggest capturing events through a custom EventBridge pipeline instead.

So my answer is that MediaConnect doesn't emit native CloudWatch Logs — there's no vended log group for flows. The closest log-equivalent diagnostic surfaces are CloudTrail, which records API activity, and EventBridge, which provides the flow event stream; CloudWatch metrics and source monitoring don't count as true log equivalents since they're dashboards rather than log records.

"}]}
